  - MUTATE F_AllCallsAuthenticated  → runs/B-L1/mutated_F_AllCallsAuthenticated.als
    rationale: Clearing this fact allows ApiCall atoms with no ac_caller (unauthenticated calls). The AuthRequiredEverywhere and FR_001_AuthRequired predicates both assert `all c: ApiCall | one c.ac_caller`, so Alloy will find a counterexample where an ApiCall atom has zero callers.
    expected to FAIL: AuthRequiredEverywhere, FR_001_AuthRequired
      - AuthRequiredEverywhere: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_001_AuthRequired: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_AppendOnlyDeletionLog  → runs/B-L1/mutated_F_AppendOnlyDeletionLog.als
    rationale: Clearing this fact removes the uniqueness constraint on td_task_ref across TaskDeletion atoms. The injection forces two distinct TaskDeletion entries with the same td_task_ref, which is exactly what AppendOnly, FR_012_PermanentDeletion, and FR_018_DeletionLogCorrectness assert cannot happen.
    expected to FAIL: AppendOnly, FR_012_PermanentDeletion, FR_018_DeletionLogCorrectness
      - AppendOnly: PASS (vacuous?)
      - FR_012_PermanentDeletion: PASS (vacuous?)
      - FR_018_DeletionLogCorrectness: PASS (vacuous?)

  - MUTATE F_ClosedTaskRule  → runs/B-L1/mutated_F_ClosedTaskRule.als
    rationale: Clearing this fact removes the constraint that editing a Done task requires reopening it. The injection forces an EditRequest targeting a Done task without a reopening status, which is exactly the violation FR_011_ClosedTaskRule checks for.
    expected to FAIL: FR_011_ClosedTaskRule
      - FR_011_ClosedTaskRule: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_AuditCompletenessOnDeletion  → runs/B-L1/mutated_F_AuditCompletenessOnDeletion.als
    rationale: Clearing this fact allows the same task to appear in multiple TaskDeletion entries (or none). The injection forces exactly two deletion log entries for the same task, violating the lone-entry requirement that AuditCompleteness asserts.
    expected to FAIL: AuditCompleteness, FR_018_DeletionLogCorrectness
      - AuditCompleteness: PASS (vacuous?)
      - FR_018_DeletionLogCorrectness: PASS (vacuous?)

  - MUTATE F_CreatorExactlyOne  → runs/B-L1/mutated_F_CreatorExactlyOne.als
    rationale: Clearing this fact allows Task atoms with no creator. The injection forces a Task with no t_creator, violating OwnershipExclusivity's assertion that every task has exactly one creator.
    expected to FAIL: OwnershipExclusivity, FR_009_CreatorRecordedImmutably, FR_017_CreatorNeverOverwritten
      - OwnershipExclusivity: PASS (vacuous?)
      - FR_009_CreatorRecordedImmutably: PASS (vacuous?)
      - FR_017_CreatorNeverOverwritten: PASS (vacuous?)

  - MUTATE F_AssigneeIsMember  → runs/B-L1/mutated_F_AssigneeIsMember.als
    rationale: Clearing this fact allows a Task to have an assignee that is not a Member. The injection forces a Task to have a non-null assignee field that does not resolve to any Member, which FR_008_AssigneeIsMember directly checks.
